  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\n\nA more significant total column push of dry air is expected this \nweekend, coinciding with a mid-level front moving through at the\nbase of the trough moving through the West. This will finally \nscour out the lingering PBL moisture across south-central AZ. \nPWATs are forecast drop as low as 0.4-0.7\" across the southern \ndeserts by Sunday. With this dry of air you can count out any\nchance at rain and count on plenty of sun. This trough will also \nhelp moderate temperatures, keeping them near to slightly above \nnormal. There is good confidence that the trough moving through \nthe West will continue on into the Plains by Monday and another\nPacific low moves to the CA coast. What this next Pacific low does\nonce reaching the CA coast Monday is a little less certain, but \nit may be what helps eventually drive moisture back up in the \ndeserts and drive the next chance at rain in the AZ deserts. \nLatest NBM shows slight PoPs (10-30%) returning by Tuesday. \nAverage to slightly above average temperatures are forecast to\ncontinue this weekend through the first half of next week with \nthis outlook, with afternoon highs around to slightly above 100 \ndegrees. With the drier air coming in, the morning lows will \nfinally be more pleasant, consistently dropping into the 70s for \nmost lower desert locations.",
